I've got a depmod error building 2.4.19 with the latest patch when I enabled 
labelled networking.

root@test:/usr/src# depmod -a -e
depmod: *** Unresolved symbols in 
/lib/modules/2.4.19lsm/kernel/security/selinux/selopt/selopt.o
depmod:         nsid_register_ops
depmod:         nsid_unregister_ops
root@test:/usr/src#

I've attached my .config.

BTW  I'm writing some programs using recvmsg_secure() so I had to use the 
experimental stuff.

For your interest, I'm writing what's basically "authbind" for SE Linux.  
It's a LD_PRELOAD hack that takes over the bind() system call and connects to 
a server via a unix domain socket sending the file descriptor and the address 
to bind() to.  The server will see the context of the client and decide 
whether to allow the bind() (in which case it will do the bind and return 
success), or whether it should be denied.

In a future version I may also take the UID/GID into account as well as the 
SE context, and I'm thinking of taking over connect() as well to bind it to a 
particular IP address.

I'm doing this to give the IP address limiting functionality of a BSD jail in 
SE Linux.

-- 
